  {
    "key": "domain.vocabulary.bob",
    "kind": "vocabulary",
    "label": "domain.vocabulary.bob",
    "description": "",
    "content": "Shared vocabulary 2026-09-24.1\nProject → optional Area → Step → Task.\nProject: Shared undertaking; distinct from a physical Building.\nPlan: Organisation of this same work, not a second work tree.\nArea: Optional grouping of Steps within a Project; not a physical Space.\nStep: Coherent work/result under Project or Area; not a Task instruction.\nTask: Assignable action with one primary Step; other links are references.\nInstruction / checkpoint: Guidance/check within a Task (task_steps); distinct from plan Steps.\nPhase: Lifecycle: concept/design/planning/build/complete; not a parent.\nStatus: Execution state; parallel active Steps are allowed. Bob focus is separate.\nFinish criterion: Evidence-backed condition for finishing a Step.\nDependency: Prerequisite; display order alone is not one.\nReadiness: Prerequisites for proceeding; distinct from phase/status/approval.\nSpace: Persistent room/space, distinct from project Area.\nSelected design: Chosen Solution revision; distinct from physical scope and attachment destination.\nDrawing / artifact: Versioned output at stated fidelity; an illustration is not measured geometry.\nNull primary_step_id means unorganised work. Preserve it. Tools define writable scope and authority.",
    "definition": {
      "role": "bob",
      "vocabulary_key": "domain.vocabulary"
    },
    "metadata": {
